---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { studioCapabilities, studioVoiceNotes } from '../../lib/studioHelp';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Studio help"
  description="Private guide to Studio voice updates and discrete prompts."
  hideFooterCta={true}
  noIndex={true}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-8 md:py-12">
    <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-gel">Private</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 font-display text-4xl text-spotlight">Studio help</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted">
      How to update the site with your voice or a short typed prompt. Reference device for
      screenshots and mic steps: <span class="text-spotlight">{studioVoiceNotes.referenceDevice}</span>.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-6 text-sm">
      <a
        href="/studio"
        class="text-gel underline-offset-2 hover:text-gold hover:underline"
      >
        ← Back to Studio
      </a>
    </p>

    <nav
      class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-2 border-b border-line pb-4 text-sm text-muted"
      aria-label="Help sections"
    >
      <a href="#getting-started" class="hover:text-gold">Getting started</a>
      <a href="#voice" class="hover:text-gold">Voice</a>
      <a href="#prompts" class="hover:text-gold">What you can say</a>
      <a href="#preview-publish" class="hover:text-gold">Preview &amp; publish</a>
      <a href="#access" class="hover:text-gold">Access</a>
    </nav>

    <section id="getting-started" class="mt-10 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl text-spotlight">Getting started</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm text-muted">
        <li>Open <a href="/studio" class="text-gel hover:text-gold">Studio</a> and sign in.</li>
        <li>
          On the hub, choose what to update — <span class="text-spotlight">Speak or type</span>,{' '}
          <span class="text-spotlight">Lesson rates</span>,{' '}
          <span class="text-spotlight">Performer facts</span>,{' '}
          <span class="text-spotlight">Reel</span>, or <span class="text-spotlight">Short bio</span>.
        </li>
        <li>
          For voice updates, hold <span class="text-spotlight">Hold to speak</span> (or type). For rates
          and facts, edit the fields directly.
        </li>
        <li>
          Tap preview, review (or tweak the fields), then <span class="text-spotlight">Publish to site</span>.
        </li>
        <li>Wait a few minutes for the site rebuild; Studio shows progress when publishing is allowed.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        You can read this help guide whenever you are signed in — even before publisher access is
        turned on.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="voice" class="mt-12 space-y-6">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl text-spotlight">Voice on iPhone</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        Voice is dictation into the Message box — not a separate command list. Speak the same kind of
        request you would type. Steps below are for {studioVoiceNotes.referenceDevice}.
      </p>

      <figure class="space-y-3">
        <img
          src="/images/studio-help/studio-help-hold-to-speak.jpg"
          alt="iPhone 17 Safari showing Studio with a finger holding the Hold to speak button while a booking message appears in the Message field."
          class="w-full max-w-sm mx-auto rounded-sm border border-line"
          width="1080"
          height="1920"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption class="text-xs text-muted text-center">
          Hold <span class="text-spotlight">Hold to speak</span>, say your update, then release.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="space-y-3 text-sm text-muted">
        <h3 class="font-display text-xl text-spotlight">Hold to speak</h3>
        <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>Open Studio in Safari on your iPhone.</li>
          <li>Press and hold <span class="text-spotlight">Hold to speak</span> (do not just tap).</li>
          <li>Keep holding while you talk. The button shows Listening…</li>
          <li>Lift your finger when you finish. Your words fill the Message box.</li>
          <li>Edit by typing if needed, then tap <span class="text-spotlight">Preview update</span>.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>{studioVoiceNotes.replacesNotAppends}</p>
        <p>{studioVoiceNotes.fallback}</p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-3 text-sm text-muted">
        <h3 class="font-display text-xl text-spotlight">Allow the microphone (first time)</h3>
        <figure class="space-y-3">
          <img
            src="/images/studio-help/studio-help-safari-mic.jpg"
            alt="iPhone 17 Safari system alert: elysetindall.com would like to access the microphone, with Don’t Allow and Allow."
            class="w-full max-w-sm mx-auto rounded-sm border border-line"
            width="1080"
            height="1920"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption class="text-xs text-muted text-center">
            Tap <span class="text-spotlight">Allow</span> when Safari asks for the microphone.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>The first time you hold <span class="text-spotlight">Hold to speak</span>, Safari asks for microphone access.</li>
          <li>Tap <span class="text-spotlight">Allow</span>.</li>
          <li>
            If you chose Don’t Allow, open the iPhone <span class="text-spotlight">Settings</span> app
            → <span class="text-spotlight">Apps</span> → <span class="text-spotlight">Safari</span> →
            <span class="text-spotlight">Microphone</span> (or Settings → Safari → scroll to
            elysetindall.com under Website Settings) and turn microphone access on, then reload Studio.
          </li>
          <li>
            Also check the Control Center mic privacy indicator and that Silent Mode / Focus is not
            blocking Safari prompts.
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          If the button reads <span class="text-spotlight">Voice not supported</span> or
          <span class="text-spotlight">Mic unavailable — type instead</span>, use the keyboard — publishing
          still works the same way.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="prompts" class="mt-12 space-y-6">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl text-spotlight">What you can say</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        Speak or type a clear request. Studio maps it to one of these updates. Include names, dates,
        venues, and prices when they matter — it will not invent credits for you.
      </p>

      <ul class="space-y-8">
        {
          studioCapabilities.map((cap) => (
            <li class="border-b border-line pb-8 last:border-0">
              <h3 class="font-display text-2xl text-spotlight">{cap.title}</h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">{cap.summary}</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-gel">
                Lives at {cap.livePath}
              </p>
              <p class="mt-4 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-muted">Try saying</p>
              <ul class="mt-2 space-y-2">
                {cap.examplePrompts.map((prompt) => (
                  <li class="rounded-sm border border-line bg-panel/40 px-3 py-2 text-sm text-spotlight">
                    “{prompt}”
                  </li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>

      <div class="rounded-sm border border-line bg-panel/40 p-4 text-sm text-muted space-y-2">
        <p class="font-semibold text-spotlight">Teaching brand reminder</p>
        <p>
          Private lessons are <span class="text-spotlight">voice lessons</span> only — vocal pedagogy,
          vocal health, and CCM. Do not ask Studio to advertise acting lessons, monologue coaching, or
          scene study.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="preview-publish" class="mt-12 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl text-spotlight">Preview &amp; publish</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm text-muted">
        <li>
          <span class="text-spotlight">Preview</span> drafts the change without going live. For rates,
          reel, bio, and facts, Preview is a <span class="text-spotlight">read-only confirmation</span>
          — go Back to edit if something looks wrong. Speak-or-type drafts for credits and news can still
          be adjusted in Preview.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="text-spotlight">Publish to site</span> commits the change. The live site updates
          after the rebuild finishes (usually a few minutes). Studio shows pipeline status and links to
          affected pages.
        </li>
        <li>Use <span class="text-spotlight">Start another update</span> when you are ready for the next change.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        Choose a job from the Studio hub, edit the values (or speak/type), then confirm in Preview and
        publish. You don’t edit website files.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="access" class="mt-12 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl text-spotlight">Who can use what</h2>
      <dl class="space-y-4 text-sm text-muted">
        <div>
          <dt class="text-spotlight">Signed in</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1">
            Open Studio and this help guide. Sign-in alone does not turn on publishing.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="text-spotlight">Publisher access</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1">
            Preview and publish require your account on the publisher list. If you see that you can’t
            publish yet, share the on-screen reference code with an admin — you can still use this help
            page to practice wording requests.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <p class="mt-12 border-t border-line pt-6 text-sm">
      <a
        href="/studio"
        class="inline-flex rounded-sm bg-gold px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-ink hover:brightness-110"
      >
        Open Studio
      </a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
